{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/reviews/id428697544"}, "name":{"label":"grimbeard95"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-24T07:05:46-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1622998972"}, "title":{"label":"I use Things for all things!"}, "content":{"label":"Things is hands-down the best app for getting organised and keeping track of tasks! To quote Chewbacca Mom, this is \"WORTH EVERY PENNY\"!\n\nIf anyone has needed an app to do as described above, the first link I send back is immediately to Things 3!\n\nLove the redesign - keep it going! 😎😎✌🏼", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/reviews/id126654764"}, "name":{"label":"Davo10001"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-24T00:30:23-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1622682948"}, "title":{"label":"Very very good. Just one little improvement needed"}, "content":{"label":"I love it. I have left Omnifocus 2 and come to Things. It's clean, straightforward and let's you get on with your day instead of fiddling with your task manager. \nOne missing thing is allowing repeating tasks to sit in projects. Their website says this is coming though. Being that and it'll be worth ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/reviews/id118077129"}, "name":{"label":"GregMW"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-23T22:38:28-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1622578980"}, "title":{"label":"Great upgrade"}, "content":{"label":"Things 3 is a great upgrade from Things 2 (nb. I use it on iPhone, iPad and Mac, so its the integrated experience I am speaking from). The addition of headings in projects and the capacity to create checklists in To Do items significantly expands the complexity of the projects that Things can handle elegantly - it's (appropriately) not as heavy duty as OmniFocus, but it covers a wider range of use cases than Things 2. The processes for adding To Dos on iOS is very elegant - easy and powerful. Things 2 has been my daily task management tool for years, and Things 3 is doing the job better.  Very happy with it. One point to note though: unlike Things 2, the iPhone app does not currently have a landscape mode. That adds friction when task titles are complex, as they sometimes are in my work, because you have to tap items one at a time to be clear what the To Do is about. It's not a showstopper for me, but I am hoping Cultured Code will address this in a further point release.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/au/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
